──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SURFACE PARITY — what was ported from the web source (no scope narrowing)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
• Composition : the AIFeatureCard scaffold — title ("Helix log/trace summary") + the cyan "Helix" badge
                (AILogTraceHelixBadge, sparkles pill) + the grounded-summary description + the Summarize
                action (visible "Ask Helix", per-surface "Summarize" verb as a11y label + the streaming
                swap to "Helix is thinking…") + the streamed-output panel (AILogTraceOutputView) — every
                region of AILogTraceSummarization.tsx and the card it renders inside.
• Window logic: web `haveWindow` / `windowSeconds` / `windowAcceptable` ported verbatim into
                AILogTraceWindow (both bounds present, start > 0, end > start, span ≤ 24h). The Summarize
                `disabled` stays a COMPUTED expression (AILogTraceSummarize.canSummarize = windowAcceptable
                && phase != streaming) — never a literal — exactly per the web render contract.
• Request body: web `body` useMemo ported into AILogTraceRequestBody.build — the zeroed `{from_unix:0,
                to_unix:0}` envelope when the window is unusable, otherwise from_unix / to_unix + the
                optional positive vehicle_id. Posted to the bare "/ai/system/logs/summarize" (the client
                prepends /api/v1, same as useAiStream). Deterministic sorted-key JSON, contract-asserted.
• Stream/out  : useAiStream `state` (idle→streaming→done/error) ported into AILogTraceStreamPhase; the web
                AiOutputPanel `hasAnything` + error/thinking/text branch selection ported into
                AILogTraceOutput.resolve; the AIThinkingIndicator (Helix label + shimmering prose lines)
                ported into AILogTraceThinkingView. Double-submit is coalesced (summarize() is a no-op while
                streaming or when the window is unusable), mirroring the hook.
• Off-mode    : web `withAiFeature('log-trace-summarization', …)` → the `gated` phase renders nothing
                (ADR-015 — the ONE intentionally empty branch; the feature slug is unit-pinned).
• States      : gated / loading (skeleton card chrome) / empty (no acceptable window → Summarize disabled +
                friendly hint, never blank) / ready (Summarize enabled) / error (parent-feed QueryError peer
                + retry), PLUS the orthogonal connection axis live/stale/offline (freshness chip + banner +
                one-shot stale auto-refresh) — the P4 leaf contract. The stream lifecycle (idle/streaming/
                done/error → hidden/thinking/text/error output) layers on top of `ready`.
• i18n        : 100% via the P1/S10 facade (AILogTraceStrings, table "AILogTraceSummarization", 20 keys = 4
                web-source + 6 shared-Helix-scaffold + 10 native chrome); zero English literals in Swift
                beyond the web-default fallbacks (the established AIRestorePanel/0201 pattern).
• Telemetry   : P1/S11 `view.opened` emitted once with surface slug "AILogTraceSummarization".
• a11y        : VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (Summarize w/ "Ask Helix · Summarize", refresh,
                retry), the output panel as an aria-live status (AILogTraceAccessibility.outputLabel), the
                card container summary (title + description), Dynamic Type via Font.TS roles, Reduce-Motion-
                aware shimmer + symbolEffect pulse.

